{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>To bless the people.</b> As is found in tractate Sotah (32a): Six tribes ascended to the top of Mount Gerizim and six to the top of Mount Ebal, and the priests and the Levites and the Ark below in the middle. The Levites turned their faces toward Mount Gerizim and opened with the blessing: ״Blessed be the man who does not make a carved or molten image,״ and these and those answer Amen. They turned back and turned their faces toward Mount Ebal and opened with the curse, saying: ״Cursed be the man who makes a carved image,״ and so all of them until ״Cursed be he who does not uphold.״"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:31.794431662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}